import ../../../ui/source_annotations.dl
import ../../../ui/application.dl

document example:
    editor "Source" containing "😀 go\nnext" using no UI appearance

set owned to an instance of example
set instance to the address of owned
set node to the control labeled "Source" in instance
set document to a UI source document named "test.dl" at "file:///test.dl" prefixed by "# hidden\n😀 " containing "😀 go\nnext" using UI CPU analysis
free document's token types
set document's token types to a JSON array containing [a new JSON-RPC text for "comment", a new JSON-RPC text for "keyword", a new JSON-RPC text for "variable"]
free document's tokens
set document's tokens to a JSON object containing [JSON child "data" is (a JSON array containing [
    a new JSON-RPC integer for 0, a new JSON-RPC integer for 0, a new JSON-RPC integer for 8, a new JSON-RPC integer for 0, a new JSON-RPC integer for 0,
    a new JSON-RPC integer for 1, a new JSON-RPC integer for 3, a new JSON-RPC integer for 2, a new JSON-RPC integer for 2, a new JSON-RPC integer for 0,
    a new JSON-RPC integer for 0, a new JSON-RPC integer for 3, a new JSON-RPC integer for 2, a new JSON-RPC integer for 1, a new JSON-RPC integer for 0,
    a new JSON-RPC integer for 1, a new JSON-RPC integer for 0, a new JSON-RPC integer for 4, a new JSON-RPC integer for 2, a new JSON-RPC integer for 0
])]
set document's token revision to document's revision
apply UI source colors from document to node in instance using (the default UI source token theme)
set value to the UI value for node in instance
require condition ((value's colors' start = 0) and (value's colors' end = 4)) reporting "An astral character was not mapped from UTF-16 to UTF-8."
require condition ((value's colors' next's start = 5) and (value's colors' next's end = 7)) reporting "A same-line prefix shifted visible tokens."
require condition ((value's last color's start = 8) and (value's last color's end = 12)) reporting "A multiline prefix shifted the last token."
require condition (value's colors' next's next = value's last color) reporting "A hidden import token leaked into the editor."
set position to the UI analysis position for source byte 5 in document
require condition (((the JSON number named "line" in position) = 1.0) and ((the JSON number named "character" in position) = 6.0)) reporting "A source request did not map its cursor through the shared prefix and Unicode mapper."
free position
set diagnostic to a JSON object containing [JSON text "message" is "Unknown name", JSON number "severity" is 1, JSON child "range" is (an LSP range from line 1 and character 6 to line 1 and character 8)]
set range to the UI source range of diagnostic in document
require condition ((range's start = 5) and (range's end = 7)) reporting "Diagnostic ranges did not use the same source mapping as colors."
free document's diagnostics
set document's diagnostics to a JSON array containing [diagnostic]
set document's diagnostic revision to document's revision
set document's diagnostic project revision to document's project's revision
require condition ((the UI source diagnostic text of document) = "test.dl:1:4: Unknown name\n") reporting "Diagnostics exposed the hidden source wrapper or counted an emoji as one UTF-16 unit."
set hidden to a JSON object containing [JSON text "message" is "Missing vocabulary", JSON child "range" is (an LSP range from line 0 and character 0 to line 0 and character 8)]
set span to the UI source range of hidden in document
require condition (span's visible = false) reporting "A project-context error was attributed to visible source."
free document's diagnostics
set document's diagnostics to a JSON array containing [hidden]
require condition ((the UI source diagnostic text of document) = "test.dl (project context): Missing vocabulary\n") reporting "A hidden import error invented a visible source location."

# Tokens without a theme rule keep the editor's authored foreground.
free document's token types
set document's token types to a JSON array containing [a new JSON-RPC text for "operator"]
free document's tokens
set document's tokens to a JSON object containing [JSON child "data" is (a JSON array containing [
    a new JSON-RPC integer for 1, a new JSON-RPC integer for 3, a new JSON-RPC integer for 2, a new JSON-RPC integer for 0, a new JSON-RPC integer for 0
])]
apply UI source colors from document to node in instance using (the default UI source token theme)
require condition (value's colors = (0 as a pointer to UI text color span)) reporting "An unstyled token replaced the editor foreground with a fixed color"
set wildcard to [@intrinsic("construct", UI source token style, "*", UI ink 12 34 56)]
apply UI source colors from document to node in instance using wildcard
require condition ((value's colors' ink's red = 12) and (value's colors' end = 4)) reporting "An explicit wildcard color did not style the unmatched token"

free document's token types
set document's token types to a JSON array containing [a new JSON-RPC text for "variable", a new JSON-RPC text for "function", a new JSON-RPC text for "operator"]
free document's token modifiers
set document's token modifiers to a JSON array containing [a new JSON-RPC text for "callDepth0"]
free document's tokens
set document's tokens to a JSON object containing [JSON child "data" is (a JSON array containing [
    a new JSON-RPC integer for 1, a new JSON-RPC integer for 3, a new JSON-RPC integer for 2, a new JSON-RPC integer for 0, a new JSON-RPC integer for 0,
    a new JSON-RPC integer for 0, a new JSON-RPC integer for 3, a new JSON-RPC integer for 2, a new JSON-RPC integer for 1, a new JSON-RPC integer for 1,
    a new JSON-RPC integer for 1, a new JSON-RPC integer for 0, a new JSON-RPC integer for 4, a new JSON-RPC integer for 2, a new JSON-RPC integer for 0
])]
mark UI text (document's source) in layer "execution" at priority 10 in node in instance
add UI text mark (UI ink 40 90 150) from 8 to 12 with opacity 80 in layer "execution" in node in instance
apply UI source colors from document to node in instance using (the light UI source token theme)
require condition ((value's colors' ink's red = 54) and (value's last color's ink's red = 48)) reporting "The light source theme lost its base or canonical nested-call colors"
require condition ((value's last color's ink's green = 79) and (value's last color's ink's blue = 195)) reporting "The light call palette did not follow the compiler's canonical colors"
require condition ((value's colors' next = value's last color) and (value's last color's end = 7)) reporting "The light theme colored an unmatched token"
apply UI source colors from document to node in instance using (the default UI source token theme)
require condition ((value's colors' ink's red = 159) and (value's last color's ink's red = 184)) reporting "Switching back to the dark source theme retained light colors"
set execution to the UI text mark layer named "execution" in node in instance
require condition ((execution's marks' start = 8) and (execution's marks' ink's red = 40)) reporting "Switching source themes changed the execution overlay"
edit UI source document document to (the string form of "changed") at 2.0 seconds
set the text of "Source" in instance to "changed"
apply UI source colors from document to node in instance using (the default UI source token theme)
require condition (value's colored text = "😀 go\nnext") reporting "Stale analysis was painted on an edited document."
free UI source project (document's project)
close instance
print line "Shared source colors and diagnostics map hidden prefixes and Unicode without touching execution marks."
